 "provenance": {
  "oracle": "YAeHMOP bind 3.1.0b2 (built from source on lenovo)",
  "why": "the 3d basis: Si, P, S and Cl carry ICON8 parameters in full, so this is the only fixture that exercises s-d, p-d and d-d overlaps",
  "parameters": "ICON8 (QCPE 517) for Si, P, S and Cl — s, p AND d — so both sides run one parameter set for these elements (P s -18.6/1.600, p -14.0/1.600, 3d -7.0/1.400; Cl s -30.0/2.033, p -15.0/2.033, 3d -9.0/2.033). Patched into a copy of the shipped table from ICON8 BLOCK DATA (/tmp/eht_parms_icon8.dat) and handed to bind with BIND_PARM_FILE.",
  "k": 1.75,
  "hij": "nonweighted (Hoffmann plain form)",
  "frame": "the app example geometry ALIGNED to its principal axes; PCl5 is a trigonal bipyramid, so its frame is well conditioned",
  "note": "bind prints the UPPER triangle of S and leaves the rest zero; the matrix here is mirrored from it. Matrices print to 4 decimals, so the comparison floor is ~2e-4 in S and ~0.05 eV in the highest virtuals, with the occupied ladder tighter. The ORBITAL ORDER above is read off bind's own orbital mapping, not from the app (bind spells two of the d functions '3dx2y2' and '3z2'; the app prints '3dx2-y2' and '3dz2').",
  "generated": "2026-09-30"
 },
